*For every cube $k\ge k_0$ and every parity instance, suppose a function $$F_Q:\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}(L_Q,\mathcal V)\longrightarrow K$$ is given for every $Q\in\mathcal Q_k$. Assume folding for every such $Q$, every $P\in\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}(L_Q,\mathcal V)$, and every $c\in K$, and assume sharing for every permitted projection $\bar\pi:L_U\to L_O$ and every $P'\in\mathop{\mathrm{Hom}}(L_O,\mathcal V)$: $$\begin{aligned}
 F_Q(P+c e_0^\top)&=F_Q(P)+c,\\
 F_U(P'\bar\pi)&=F_O(P').
 \end{aligned}
 \label{eq:matrix-family-identities}$$ If this family passes the table test of Equation <a href="#eq:matrix-test" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:matrix-test">[eq:matrix-test]</a> with probability at least $0.99$, then the projected advice experiment with $\beta=k^{-2/3}$ has local strategies whose probability of full answer agreement is at least $\gamma$.

