outputs.exact_statement:
For every fixed $\varepsilon,\delta\in(0,1/2)$, there are an integer $s\ge1$ and a deterministic polynomial-time reduction from $\mathrm{3SAT}$ to explicit unweighted Unique Games instances $G_\varphi$ over $K=\mathbb F_2^s$ such that $$\begin{aligned}
 \varphi\text{ satisfiable}
 &\quad\Longrightarrow\quad \mathop{\mathrm{val}}(G_\varphi)\ge1-\varepsilon,\\
 \varphi\text{ unsatisfiable}
 &\quad\Longrightarrow\quad \mathop{\mathrm{val}}(G_\varphi)\le\delta.
\end{aligned}$$ The graph is simple and bipartite, and every constraint is a translation $a(v_e)=a(u_e)+c_e$ of $K$. The alphabet, the degree of the running-time polynomial, and its constants depend only on $\varepsilon,\delta$.

For every $p_*>0$ there is an integer $r_*$ such that, for every sufficiently large integer $\ell$, the following objects exist: a finite-dimensional binary space $\mathcal V$ containing an identified subspace $K=\mathbb F_2^\ell$, a map $C:\mathcal V\to K$, and a rational probability distribution $\mu$ on $\mathcal V$. They satisfy $$\label{eq:latent-equivariance}
 C(x+k)=C(x)+k
 \qquad(x\in\mathcal V,\ k\in K),$$ and, for independent uniform $x\in\mathcal V$ and $a\sim\mu$, $$\label{eq:latent-small-change}
 \Pr[C(x+a)\ne C(x)]\le p_*.$$ Moreover, every linear subspace $G\le\mathcal V^*$ with $\dim(G|_K)\ge r_*$ satisfies $$\label{eq:latent-detection}
 \Pr_{a\sim\mu}[\text{there exists }g\in G\text{ with }g(a)\ne0]
 \ge\frac18.$$ In particular, $r_*$ is fixed before $\ell$ is chosen. For rational $p_*$, the threshold and all the finite data can be found by a terminating deterministic algorithm.

For independent uniform $u\in P_t$ and noise $\xi_t$, $$\label{eq:latent-change-probability}
 p_t:=\Pr[C_t(u+\xi_t)\ne C_t(u)]
     =(1-q^{-3})(1-\theta)^t.$$

Set $$\label{eq:latent-depth}
 s=\left\lfloor\frac{H_{r_0}}{8\theta}\right\rfloor.$$ Every full lift on $P_s$ detects $\xi_s$ with probability at least $1/4$: $$\label{eq:latent-full-lift-detection}
 \Pr[\text{there exists }z\in B^*\text{ with }\psi_z(\xi_s)\ne0]
 \ge\frac14.$$

Choose the latent and shortcode parameters in the order specified by Equation <a href="#eq:matrix-parameters" data-reference-type="eqref" data-reference="eq:matrix-parameters">[eq:matrix-parameters]</a>, fixing $\mathcal V=K\oplus W$ before $k$. There are a constant $\gamma>0$ and an integer $k_0\ge8$, depending only on these fixed parameters, with the following property.*


